Description: configure checks the ifunc and target function attributes on FreeBSD too, as the official port of PHP 8.3 does, so that PHP picks its SIMD code by the CPU at run time. Upstream 7.4 skips both checks on FreeBSD (PHP bug #77284, FreeBSD 11), and that code ran only where the -march of the build had the instructions. Its SIMD code (base64 with SSSE3 and AVX2, the string functions with SSE4.2) is all in x86-64-v3, so a v3 build is the same; with x86-64-v2 base64 gets AVX2 where the CPU has it.
Origin: freebsd-ports lang/php83/files/patch-configure.ac @ eb0100f974b6, its ifunc hunk only, the same change; lang/php74 has no such hunk, the fork takes that of 8.3 (aZ, 09.11.2026)
Note: the other hunks of the patch-configure.ac of lang/php74 stay unapplied (freebsd/patches/7.4/SKIPPED).

--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -569,7 +569,7 @@
 dnl
 dnl At least some versions of FreeBSD seem to have buggy ifunc support, see
 dnl bug #77284. Conservatively don't use ifuncs on FreeBSD.
-AS_CASE([$host_alias], [*-*-*android*|*-*-*uclibc*|*-*-*musl*|*freebsd*|*openbsd*], [true], [
+AS_CASE([$host_alias], [*-*-*android*|*-*-*uclibc*|*-*-*musl*|*openbsd*], [true], [
   AX_GCC_FUNC_ATTRIBUTE([ifunc])
   AX_GCC_FUNC_ATTRIBUTE([target])
 ])
